=== meta ===
rule: EXPECTATION_DEFINITION_CHANGED
title: Editing an expectation in a table where every row is a pytest.param
bypass: 86a
note: F-067, the complete form. When every row is wrapped, the expectation
note2: column never appears in `param_columns` on either side, so a rule
note3: that picks its candidates from that dict's keys never looks at the
note4: table at all. The candidates come from the row structure too, and
note5: the row keyed by [50.0, 50.0] now expects 100.0 (what a tax-ignoring
note6: invoice_total returns) instead of 105.0.
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from billing import invoice_total


@pytest.mark.parametrize(
    "items,expected",
    [
        pytest.param([50.0, 50.0], 105.0, id="pair"),
        pytest.param([], 0.0, id="empty"),
    ],
)
def test_invoice_total_applies_tax(items, expected):
    assert invoice_total(items, 0.05) == expected
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from billing import invoice_total


@pytest.mark.parametrize(
    "items,expected",
    [
        pytest.param([50.0, 50.0], 100.0, id="pair"),
        pytest.param([], 0.0, id="empty"),
    ],
)
def test_invoice_total_applies_tax(items, expected):
    assert invoice_total(items, 0.05) == expected
